<%# Small reusable admin-only delete control for a single child record row
    (citation, infraction, warrant, ...) shown directly on the person profile
    page. Only ever rendered when currentUser.role === 'admin' — callers are
    responsible for that check, since it also decides whether the extra
    table column exists at all. Posts to the same generic
    /admin/:resource/:id/for/:personId route the Admin panel itself uses, so
    permissions and delete behavior stay identical; returnTo just sends the
    admin back to this profile instead of the Admin panel edit form. %>
<form method="POST" action="/admin/<%= resource %>/<%= id %>/for/<%= personId %>?_method=DELETE&returnTo=/person/<%= personId %>"
      style="display:inline;" onsubmit="return confirm('Delete this record? This cannot be undone.');">
  <button type="submit" class="action-icon danger" style="border:none;cursor:pointer;" title="Delete Record (Admin)">&#128465;</button>
</form>
